---
import { taxPrinciples, taxProgramGroups, taxSourceLinks } from '../data/taxPrograms';
---

<section id="tax-architecture" class="relative scroll-mt-32 border-y border-hairline bg-paper-soft/45 py-14 md:py-24">
  <div class="section-shell">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-7 md:grid-cols-[180px_1fr] md:gap-14">
      <p class="coord pt-1">04 / Tax architecture</p>
      <div>
        <h2 class="section-heading max-w-3xl text-3xl md:text-5xl">
          The hidden layer is after-tax structure.
        </h2>
        <p class="section-copy mt-5 max-w-3xl text-base md:text-lg">
          This is not loophole chasing. It is structural literacy: entity choice, holding period,
          basis, account wrapper, income year, and geography can decide how much of an idea
          actually compounds.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="dossier-panel mt-10 overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:mt-14">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[0.88fr_1.12fr]">
        <div class="border-b border-hairline p-5 md:border-b-0 md:border-r md:p-7">
          <p class="coord text-accent">Why it belongs</p>
          <h3 class="mt-4 max-w-lg font-sans text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">
            Tax is the finance lens turned into architecture.
          </h3>
          <p class="section-copy mt-5 text-base md:text-lg">
            Alex already thinks in systems: entertainment has production structure, geospatial work
            has physical structure, and finance has ownership structure. Tax-aware planning is the
            same instinct applied to the final outcome: who owns the upside, when it is realized,
            where it sits, and what wrapper lets it compound.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-7 border-t border-hairline pt-5">
            <p class="coord text-signal">Portfolio framing</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft md:text-base">
              The public site should present this as a research and planning map, not personal tax
              advice. The signal is that Alex knows where structure can matter and knows when the
              answer needs a specialist.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 md:p-7">
          <p class="coord text-accent">Four levers</p>
          <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            {taxPrinciples.map((principle) => (
              <div class="border-t border-hairline pt-4">
                <h4 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">
                  {principle.title}
                </h4>
                <p class="section-copy mt-3 text-sm">
                  {principle.body}
                </p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
      {taxProgramGroups.map((group) => (
        <section class="surface-quiet rounded-md p-5 md:p-6">
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 border-b border-hairline pb-5">
            <p class="coord text-accent">{group.title}</p>
            <p class="section-copy text-sm md:text-base">
              {group.angle}
            </p>
          </div>

          <ul class="divide-y divide-hairline">
            {group.programs.map((program) => (
              <li class="py-5">
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-start sm:justify-between">
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">
                      {program.name}
                    </h3>
                    <p class="mono mt-2 text-xs uppercase text-ink-muted">
                      {program.code}
                    </p>
                  </div>
                  <span class="mono inline-flex w-fit rounded-sm border border-hairline bg-paper-soft px-2 py-1 text-xs text-signal">
                    {program.status}
                  </span>
                </div>

                <p class="section-copy mt-4 text-sm">
                  {program.fit}
                </p>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
                  <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Best fit:</span> {program.use}
                </p>
                <a
                  href={program.sourceHref}
                  class="mt-4 inline-flex text-sm font-medium text-accent underline decoration-accent/35 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-ink"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noreferrer"
                >
                  {program.sourceLabel}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="ledger-rule mt-6 rounded-md p-5 md:p-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] lg:items-start">
        <div>
          <p class="coord text-signal">Current as a research map</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            Tax law changes, state conformity matters, and implementation details are everything.
            This section is a planning lens, not tax advice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          {taxSourceLinks.map((source) => (
            <a
              href={source.href}
              class="button-secondary"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
            >
              {source.label}
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
